## What happened

PR #134 was still based on `position-theory-mediated-lineage` when it was merged. PR #132 had already been squash-merged into `main`, so merging #134 updated the old feature branch rather than `main`. The rendered article therefore contains the lineage expansion from #132 but not the structural edit from #134.

## This repair

This branch was created directly from the current `main` tip after #132. It reapplies only the intended article state from #134, producing a clean one-file diff against `main`.

The article:

- follows the six bounded units defined in `article-roles.md`;
- keeps the opening focused on the central question, learning unit, theory mediation, testbeds, and the human-inclusive evidence disclosure;
- places the two-lineage positioning after the fallible-search mechanism;
- moves operator reallocation and cut-set language to the bootstrap discussion, while routing the full derivation to the decisions companion;
- combines the evidence ladder with truth-versus-fit evaluation;
- combines the recorded episode with the proposed intervention and longitudinal study;
- removes the standalone Sutton section and routes the full scaling argument to the Bitter Lesson companion;
- preserves the alternatives and abandonment conditions.

This is a restack/repair only: no new theory changes beyond the already-reviewed #134 content.
